{"id":"v4","level":4,"levelName":"The verb system","n":5,"of":10,"title":"Having it happen to you","titleHe":"בִּנְיַן נִפְעַל","goal":"Recognise nif'al, the passive counterpart of pa'al.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"נִפְעַל is what pa'al becomes when the subject is on the receiving end. Its present and past both begin with נִ, which makes it the easiest binyan to spot — and the easiest to confuse with itself, since נִכְנַס is both he entered and he enters."},{"type":"binyan","he":"נִפְעַל","en":"nif'al","note":"The passive or reflexive counterpart of pa'al.","verb":{"root":"כ־נ־ס","inf":"לְהִכָּנֵס","en":"to enter, to go in"},"tense":"present","rows":[{"label":"masculine singular","he":"","form":"נִכְנָס"},{"label":"feminine singular","he":"","form":"נִכְנֶסֶת"},{"label":"masculine plural","he":"","form":"נִכְנָסִים"},{"label":"feminine plural","he":"","form":"נִכְנָסוֹת"}]},{"type":"binyan","he":"נִפְעַל","en":"nif'al","note":"The passive or reflexive counterpart of pa'al.","verb":{"root":"כ־נ־ס","inf":"לְהִכָּנֵס","en":"to enter, to go in"},"tense":"past","rows":[{"label":"I","he":"אֲנִי","form":"נִכְנַסְתִּי"},{"label":"you (m.)","he":"אַתָּה","form":"נִכְנַסְתָּ"},{"label":"you (f.)","he":"אַתְּ","form":"נִכְנַסְתְּ"},{"label":"he","he":"הוּא","form":"נִכְנַס"},{"label":"she","he":"הִיא","form":"נִכְנְסָה"},{"label":"we","he":"אֲנַחְנוּ","form":"נִכְנַסְנוּ"},{"label":"you (m.pl.)","he":"אַתֶּם","form":"נִכְנַסְתֶּם"},{"label":"you (f.pl.)","he":"אַתֶּן","form":"נִכְנַסְתֶּן"},{"label":"they","he":"הֵם / הֵן","form":"נִכְנְסוּ"}]},{"type":"tip","body":"Many nif'al verbs aren't passive in meaning at all — נִכְנָס enters, נִשְׁאָר stays, נִמְצָא is located. Treat the pattern as a shape first and a meaning second."}],"vocab":[{"he":"נִכְנָס","en":"enters","translit":"nichnas"},{"he":"נִמְצָא","en":"is located, is found","translit":"nimtsa"},{"he":"נִשְׁאָר","en":"stays, remains","translit":"nish'ar"},{"he":"נִרְאֶה","en":"seems, looks","translit":"nir'e"},{